index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..28543ca31aa88fbc6d12962008345162fed2e2c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/C1-DECLARED-TARGET-LEARNABILITY-V2-2026-09-10.md
@@ -0,0 +1,201 @@
+**The repaired-schema sealed C1 head achieves LOAO top-1 `0.3381` versus the `0.1716` floor and LOAO level `R² = 0.0379`, so the result supports the fixed second reading: the v1 verdict was an artefact of the defective schema.**
+
+`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`
+
+## Answer
+
+[RUN] On the same 37 modeled exact-path anchors, changing Q1 from the defective
+16-slot v1 representation to `mcrl-v025-stagec-q1-action-v2` changes the sealed
+width-8 head's LOAO top-1 accuracy from `0.1711` to `0.3381`, a gain of
+`+0.1670`; the unchanged constant floor is `0.1716`. Its raw held-out level
+`R²` changes from `−0.2724` to `0.0379`, a gain of `+0.3102`. LOAO ordering
+changes from `0.5889` to `0.7310`, a gain of `+0.1421`.
+
+[INFERRED] Under the reading fixed before the run, these are material movements.
+The result therefore supports **“the v1 verdict was an artefact of the defective
+schema.”** It does not support the first reading that the ceiling is really
+informational. This conclusion is about the v1 learnability verdict, not EE and
+not production readiness.
+
+## Evidence labels and scope
+
+- `[RUN]` means verified by running the required interpreter against the current
+  code and data.
+- `[DERIVED]` means arithmetic or algebra applied to the run outputs and declared
+  definitions.
+- `[INFERRED]` is the interpretation required by the fixed reading.
+
+[RUN] No production training, policy run, acceptance test, or EE endpoint ran.
+Loss values are not used as EE evidence. This job makes no EE claim. No sealed
+constant, threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard, acceptance rule, control
+law, manifest, or optimizer setting was changed.
+
+## Requested v1/v2 table
+
+[RUN] Values are pooled held-out metrics. Parentheses are 2,000-replicate
+anchor-bootstrap intervals for the sealed primary where the v1 report supplied
+one. `[DERIVED]` Every delta is `v2 − v1`; `—` means the original requested
+summary cell had no value, so no numeric delta exists.
+
+| statistic | sealed `(8,)` v1 | sealed `(8,)` v2 | Δ | flexible nonlinear v1 | flexible nonlinear v2 | Δ | floor v1 | floor v2 | Δ |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| LOAO ordering | `0.5889` `[0.5658, 0.6115]` | `0.7310` `[0.7090, 0.7535]` | `+0.1421`; interval endpoints `+0.1432`, `+0.1420` | `0.6197` | `0.6954` | `+0.0756` | `0.5000` | `0.5000` | `0.0000` |
+| LOAO level `R²` | `−0.2724` `[−0.5750, −0.0435]` | `0.0379` `[−0.0485, 0.1050]` | `+0.3102`; interval endpoints `+0.5265`, `+0.1485` | `0.0933` | `0.1287` | `+0.0353` | — | — | — |
+| top-1 accuracy | `0.1711` | `0.3381` `[0.2881, 0.3827]` | `+0.1670` | `0.1854` | `0.2746` | `+0.0892` | `0.1716` | `0.1716` | `0.0000` |
+| LOWO level `R²` | — | — | — | `−0.0714` | `−0.0902` | `−0.0189` | — | — | — |
+
+[RUN] The v2 primary top-1 bootstrap interval lies wholly above the unchanged
+constant floor. The v2 level interval crosses zero, but the fixed reading needs
+only either top-1 or level `R²` to move materially; both point estimates moved,
+and top-1 did so decisively.
+
+## Same-sample construction and power
+
+[RUN] The modeled panel is identical to v1: 37 anchors, 36,360 rows, 3,700
+`(anchor,user)` groups, and 160,444 non-tied within-group target pairs. It uses
+world 1 steps 0–17 and world 2 steps 0–18, setting `a-r0`, carrier
+`nearest-eligible`, 100 users, the shipped shortlist support, the same
+calibration, and boundary indices `(0,)`. Thus there is no unequal-sample
+comparison and no new anchor shortfall. The broader generation cache still has
+39 anchors (19 and 20 by world); as in v1, the final two are verification-only
+and excluded from modeling.
+
+[RUN] The v2 fitted panel was first made by applying the successor's deterministic
+geometry projection to the exact-path v1 parent rows used by the v1 fit. The
+parent input digests are `328ca5b2…56aae9` and `d3db1339…f248de`; their exact
+base gauge is `0.0`, target recomposition residual is at most `3.553e−15`, and
+the independent `c1_difference_surplus` residual is at most `3.469e−14`.
+Rebuilding the world tapes supplied the decision-boundary geometry; provider
+array elevation and independent ECEF elevation agreed within `5.400e−13`
+degrees.
+
+[RUN] A subsequent direct traversal of `q1_schema_v2.build_exact_rows_v2` covers
+all 37 modeled anchors. For each call the adapter sets
+`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = False` on the imported pilot module, invokes
+the exact builder, and restores the original module value. Every regenerated
+declared target, v1 parent Q1 vector, and v2 Q1 vector is compared row-for-row
+with the fitted panel. The final direct-audit counts and maximum deviations are
+reported in the reproducibility section below.
+
+[RUN] Power is unchanged from v1: 37 independent anchor clusters contribute to
+the anchor bootstrap. LOWO still has only two world clusters, so it is a
+descriptive cross-world transfer check, not a powered population-of-worlds
+estimate.
+
+## Learner and metric protocol
+
+[RUN] The sealed primary used the repository `AdamMLPHead` with the same literals:
+hidden `(8,)`, ReLU, learning rate `1.0e-2`, `gauge_beta = 0.2`, Adam betas
+`(0.9, 0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight decay, 2,000 source epochs, and one
+deterministic full-batch update per route per epoch. The deterministic aggregate
+retained 4,096 base-to-candidate pairs per fold. LOAO uses sealed learner seed
+`6407676579069309528`; seeded LOWO results are arithmetic means over the same
+four sealed seeds.
+
+[RUN] Metric definitions are unchanged: raw held-out levels with no test-time
+re-gauging for `R²`; all non-tied true pairs within held-out `(anchor,user)`
+groups for ordering, with prediction ties worth `0.5`; and stable predicted
+argmax matching any true maximum within `1e-12` for top-1.
+
+## Reference set and widths
+
+[RUN] Each cell is `v2 (Δ from v1)`. The linear model uses the same closed-form
+pairwise squared objective and `0.2` reference gauge. The flexible model is the
+same fixed-seed two-layer ReLU random-feature family, with input width changing
+only from 16 to 15; its ridge is still selected inside every outer fold from
+`{0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100, 1000}` using training-only anchor validation.
+
+| declared-target model | LOAO `R²` | LOAO order | LOAO top-1 | LOWO `R²` | LOWO order | LOWO top-1 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| constant | `−0.0058 (+0.0000)` | `0.5000 (+0.0000)` | `0.1716 (+0.0000)` | `−0.0005 (+0.0000)` | `0.5000 (+0.0000)` | `0.1716 (+0.0000)` |
+| plain linear | `−0.0221 (+0.1285)` | `0.6949 (+0.1235)` | `0.1895 (+0.1059)` | `−0.0896 (+0.1555)` | `0.6800 (+0.1221)` | `0.1965 (+0.1043)` |
+| sealed width 8 | `0.0379 (+0.3102)` | `0.7310 (+0.1421)` | `0.3381 (+0.1670)` | `−0.1605 (+0.4903)` | `0.7073 (+0.1128)` | `0.3160 (+0.1297)` |
+| width 32 | `0.0040 (+0.3106)` | `0.7385 (+0.1405)` | `0.3141 (+0.1614)` | `−0.4845 (+0.4195)` | `0.7115 (+0.1350)` | `0.3428 (+0.1441)` |
+| width 128 | `−0.1926 (+0.4914)` | `0.7138 (+0.1139)` | `0.3416 (+0.1422)` | `−1.4092 (+1.0966)` | `0.6356 (+0.0819)` | `0.2951 (+0.1107)` |
+| high-capacity 15-256-256 nonlinear basis | `0.1287 (+0.0353)` | `0.6954 (+0.0756)` | `0.2746 (+0.0892)` | `−0.0902 (−0.0189)` | `0.6799 (+0.0812)` | `0.2824 (+0.0884)` |
+
+[RUN] The decisive top-1 gain is present in the literal sealed width-8 head; it
+does not require extra width or epochs. Widening is mixed and does not explain
+the schema effect.
+
+## Repaired-coordinate permutation importance
+
+[RUN] Importance uses the high-capacity LOWO model and the unchanged v1 method:
+globally permute one coordinate inside each held-out world fold, then report the
+drop from baseline (`R² = −0.09024`, ordering `0.67989`, top-1 `0.28243`). Both
+repaired coordinates carry substantial held-out signal.
+
+| v2 slot | feature | Δ`R²` | Δordering | Δtop-1 | permuted `R²` | permuted order | permuted top-1 |
+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 5 | repaired `off_axis_angle` | `0.0943` | `0.0964` | `0.0770` | `−0.1846` | `0.5834` | `0.2054` |
+| 6 | `focal_link_elevation` | `0.1909` | `0.1414` | `0.1381` | `−0.2811` | `0.5385` | `0.1443` |
+
+[INFERRED] The repaired coordinates are not inert. Elevation is the stronger of
+the two under all three permutation metrics, and each independently removes a
+large part of the flexible model's held-out ordering/top-1 signal when broken.
+
+## Rank, condition number, and effective dimension
+
+[RUN] On the 36,360 modeled rows, using the same raw physical-unit convention as
+the schema census, the full 15-column matrix has rank `14` and infinite condition
+number because `missing_incumbent` is exactly zero. Dropping that documented
+structural coordinate gives rank `14` and condition number `1.893761e4`.
+Therefore the schema-defined effective dimension is `[DERIVED] 15 − 1 = 14`,
+matching the full-corpus census in rank, full-condition class, and effective
+dimension.
+
+[RUN] There is an additional panel-specific fact that the earlier v1 report did
+not audit: `nominal_required_power_over_cap` is exactly `1.0` on every one of
+these 36,360 exact-path rows (it is also exactly `1.0` in the corresponding v1
+panel). If “effective dimension on these rows” means the number of empirically
+varying coordinates rather than the schema/census definition, the answer is
+`13`; dropping both empirical constants gives rank `13` and condition number
+`1.893723e4`, and the mean-centered full matrix has rank `13`. The broader
+176,223-row census varies required power and therefore has 14 varying
+coordinates. This sample-specific constancy is not caused by v2 and does not
+alter the paired v1/v2 result, but it prevents claiming that every
+subset-conditioned census number matches exactly.
+
+## Reproducibility, file integrity, and resources
+
+[RUN] The required interpreter was
+`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`. All runs used `nice -n 15` and
+set OpenBLAS, OMP, MKL, BLIS, NumExpr, and vecLib thread counts to 1. The maximum
+was three Python processes (analysis parent plus two fit workers); geometry
+projection used one, and the direct two-world exact audit used two. Every Python
+process had a 5 GiB address-space hard limit, which also bounds its possible RSS
+below 5 GiB.
